+# Qwen3-30B NVFP4 TP Parity Diagnostic
+
+## Scope
+
+This diagnostic corrects the earlier Task 13 K interpretation. The previous smoke only proved:
+
+```text
+TP1 greedy generation != TP2 greedy generation
+```
+
+It did not prove full-vocab logits mismatch beyond tolerance.
+
+## Commands
+
+```bash
+conda run -n hif4 python NVFP4/scripts/diagnose_qwen3_30b_nvfp4_tp_parity.py \
+  --tp1-gpus 0 \
+  --tp2-gpus 0,7 \
+  --top-logprobs 100 \
+  --max-new-tokens 8 \
+  --summary-json /tmp/hif4_task13_tp_parity/summary_top100.json \
+  --out-dir /tmp/hif4_task13_tp_parity/top100
+```
+
+```bash
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 conda run -n hif4 python \
+  NVFP4/scripts/diagnose_qwen3_30b_nvfp4_layer_tp_puncture.py \
+  --layer 0 \
+  --tokens 4 \
+  --out-json /tmp/hif4_task13_tp_parity/layer0_puncture.json
+```
+
+## Next-Token Top-100 Raw-Logits Diagnostic
+
+This uses vLLM `logprobs_mode=raw_logits` and top-100 returned scores, not full-vocab logits.
+
+- TP1 and TP2 both used `linear_backend=emulation`, `moe_backend=emulation`, `kv_cache_dtype=bfloat16`, `enforce_eager=true`, `enable_prefix_caching=false`, `async_scheduling=false`.
+- Prefill next-token top1 matched for all 4 prompts.
+- Greedy generation still diverged for 3 of 4 prompts within 8 generated tokens.
+- First-divergence top-k overlap stayed high: top5 overlap 4-5, top10 overlap 9 for divergent prompts.
+- First-divergence shared top-100 cosine was high: about 0.9995-0.9998.
+- Divergence occurred at small or tie-like margins:
+  - `Hello`: TP1 margin 0.0, TP2 margin 0.25.
+  - `The capital of France is`: TP1 margin 0.75, TP2 margin 0.875.
+  - `Write one word: ok`: TP1 margin 0.75, TP2 margin 0.0.
+
+## Layer-Level TP Puncture
+
+Layer 0 fixed hidden tensor, full result vs TP2 shard/reduce reconstruction:
+
+```text
+q_proj max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+k_proj max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+v_proj max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+router_logits max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+W13 gate max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+W13 up max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+SwiGLU max_abs=0 rel_l2=0
+o_proj row-reduce max_abs=0.0078125 rel_l2=0.002936 nmse=8.62e-06
+W2 row-reduce max_abs=0.03125 rel_l2=0.003613 nmse=1.31e-05
+complete MoE max_abs=0.03125 rel_l2=0.003745 nmse=1.40e-05
+```
+
+Scale and sharding invariants checked:
+
+```text
+qkv_input_global_scale_inv_all_equal=true
+qkv_weight_global_scale_all_equal=true
+moe_a13_input_global_scale_inv_all_equal=true
+moe_a2_input_global_scale_inv_all_equal=true
+hidden_half_mod16=0
+q_out_half_mod16=0
+kv_out_half_mod16=0
+moe_intermediate_half_mod16=0
+router_selected_experts_equal=true
+moe_selected_experts_equal=true
+```
+
+## Current Interpretation
+
+The current evidence favors Case A: small numerical differences and small/tie-like top1/top2 margins cause greedy bifurcation. It does not prove an NVFP4 TP2 sharding or scale semantic bug.
+
+Generation exact match should remain a report item, not the first PASS/FAIL gate. Task 13 K should be evaluated as a TP1/TP2 numerical parity diagnostic before any decision to change NVFP4 emulation math.
